  "qualification_limits": [
    "Successful FRED/UIRET transitions are not exercised; their compiler identities, feature/mode rules and object bytes are verified.",
    "RSM evidence is KVM-mediated SMM using SMI-created save state and explicit code64 setup inside SMM, not bare-metal firmware qualification.",
    "CET, XSTATE, NT/task-resume returns, faults, asynchronous events/unwinding and other CPU models remain unqualified.",
    "These APIs provide named compiler inputs, not a complete original-image GPR/vector continuation. NeverD lifting and explicit-state admission remain separate contracts.",
    "NeverC stage-1 and focused regressions pass; full product CI and stage-2 qualification are not claimed.",
    "Global NeverD state, decoder and qualification gaps remain in the support table; this phase changes NeverD documentation only."
  ],
  "release_and_pins_changed": false
